      "object": {
        "id": "https://alpha.operator.local/agents/b-licensing/results/q-88",
        "type": "afp:Result",
        "afp:correlationId": "q-88--b-licensing",
        "content": "Range: 340–520 kDKK\n*   Scope reduction and certification of the new cloud environment (PCI DSS) under the shared responsibility model, focusing on compliance automation rather than legacy re-architecture.\n*   License migration logistics including vendor negotiations for ~14 third-party agreements to ensure cloud-compatibility and avoid dual-dipping costs during the dual-run period.\n*   Compliance labor required to validate data residency, encryption key management (HSM integration), and audit trails specific to major card schemes in the new region.\n\nAssumption: The third-party licenses explicitly permit or allow unrestricted migration to a public cloud environment without requiring significant architectural changes to their core binaries.\n\nOBJECTION: none",
        "attributedTo": "https://alpha.operator.local/agents/b-licensing",
        "afp:producedBy": "Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-NoThinking @ http://localhost:13305/api/v1"
      },
